  Well, after a year and a half of playing Nethack, I finally beat it.
It was a no-nonsense game, genocide everything that could get in your way, 
grab the Amulet and run like hell.  I was only level 13 with 108 HP
when I won.  Some thoughts:

 Genocide is too powerful.  By the end of the game, I remember these
things being gone.

Rust monsters
Minotaurs
All Liches
All Dragons
All jellies
Wraiths (Argh!  That scroll of blank paper must have been BLESSED!)

I think you'll agree that there's not much that's dangerous left after those
guys are gone.  And before I get any flames, dragons didn't go away 
until I was on my way up, and had all my intrinsics (never did get 
shock resistance, though, but grid bugs weren't worrying me too much).

 Rings of conflict aren't overpowered nearly as much.  They are very
useful to have, but they're not much more useful than being able to stand
in a hallway and fight one thing at a time.  The hardest monsters,
namely, the Wiz, dragons, and minotaurs, don't care much about conflict.
Wiz ignores it, dragons shoot at you from a distance, and minotaurs are 
usually alone.  

 Bones levels in hell are redundant.
 -Tom
